  "note": "Chrome CPU-throttle proxy for an iPhone XS Max (414x896 @3, mobile profile); GPU work is not throttled. Other sessions kept the host 16-58% busy, so the step-3 build (.tmp/step3/dist-step3, --sourcemap) and the final build (--sourcemap of HEAD) were alternated in one round under the same conditions. Frame means at 4x track the host-load window a run lands in; the CPU-profile cost per frame, the sampled allocation per frame and the pinned Node micro-benchmark are the direct measures. Builds labelled step4-pass-only are the first commit alone (4d5fc4eb).",
  "change": {
    "enemyRenderPass": "apps/hmh-reboot/src/enemy-render-pass.mjs (lazy chunk, 5,960 B, every dependency injected): the renderWorld enemy loop without per-enemy objects. One projection per enemy into scratch arrays (was two { ...enemy } copies plus a candidate object), a bounded max-heap for the animation budget in the exact (priority, distance, id, row) order of selectAnimatedEnemyIds (was filter/map/full sort/slice/Set), the six-state result computed once and reused, elite flag and locomotion phase cached per display by id, one reused pose and shadow object, pips in typed arrays.",
    "helpers": "worldToScreenInto (worldToScreen no longer copies the viewport), isScreenPointVisible and the pose memo without per-call arrays and closures, roster clip lookups through a nested phase/state/direction table (was four template-string keys per pose), unchanged body tints skip the sprite setter, selectEnemyRosterPose and creatureAnimationTick accept precomputed inputs.",
    "leakFix": "enemyVisualFacing gained one entry per enemy ever drawn: defeated enemies retire in the tick that kills them, so the render never saw them inactive. Marker syncs now prune it.",
    "renderCleanups": "gore render walks its pools directly (no per-frame copies, in-place pruning, one reused projected point, fragment seeds hashed once, empty layers not cleared); contact shadow placements write into one object; the static bake key fills a reused array and compares in place, with main.mjs passing a joined blocker key kept until the ids change; focus points reuse their array and points; the HUD reads run ranks directly instead of a deep-frozen progression snapshot per frame and counts enemies in one loop.",
    "tooling": "hmh-perf-crowd-bench --mode=alloc (CDP sampling heap profiler incl. collected objects, per-function bytes via source maps; aggregateHeapProfile unit-tested), scripts/hmh-restart-leak-probe.mjs, scripts/hmh-enemy-pass-bench.mjs."
  },
