  "deferred": [
    "Pixi Graphics tessellation is the largest allocator: about 2.25 MB per frame in the mobile crowd (buildLine, circle/roundRect triangulation, buildContextBatches: about half of all sampled bytes) from per-frame immediate-mode layers (health pips, elite rings, tells, gore, combat VFX, world-life, reticle). It needs pooled sprites or retained geometry, not an allocation tweak.",
    "Renderer process private memory grows outside the JS heap over a long run (see leakProbe).",
    "The hero atlas still builds string keys and a joined frame-id string per frame (one body); worldLife queries ground for every site each frame.",
    "Per-frame stage dataset writes (about 10 attribute writes) measured under 0.1% and were left as they are."
  ]
}
